00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:34.490
In an earlier season, there had been a discussion about if Pam could sometimes wear pants to the office.
在早期的某一季里，曾经讨论过帕姆是否可以偶尔在办公室穿裤子。

474
00:20:34.490 --> 00:20:39.250
Because she had such a uniform of her cardigan and her pencil skirt and everything.
因为她总是穿着开衫配铅笔裙之类的制服。

475
00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:41.630
And it went all the way up to the network.
而且这件事一直闹到了电视网高层。

476
00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:45.810
And the network said, Pam must wear pencil skirts.
电视网说，帕姆必须穿铅笔裙。

477
00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:47.390
Yeah.
是啊。

478
00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:47.910
Okay.
好吧。

479
00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:49.910
I have wondered about this, Jenna.
珍娜，我一直对此很好奇。

480
00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:51.290
And I've never told you this.
而且我从来没跟你说过。

481
00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:55.170
But for a few episodes, they put Angela Martin in dress pants.
有几集里，他们让安吉拉·马丁穿了西裤。

482
00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:55.730
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

483
00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.510
And then all of a sudden, the pants went away.
然后突然之间，裤子就不见了。

484
00:20:57.710 --> 00:21:01.010
And so I went to wardrobe and I said, hey, can we bring back the dress pants?
所以我去找服装组说，嘿，我们能把西裤穿回来吗？

485
00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:01.830
Those are so comfortable.
那些裤子太舒服了。

486
00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:05.570
And they said, oh, actually, we got a note that they just want you in skirts.
他们说，哦，其实我们收到通知，他们只想让你穿裙子。

487
00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:06.990
Isn't that interesting?
这难道不有趣吗？

488
00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:09.390
I did not know you got the same note.
我不知道你也收到了同样的通知。

489
00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:10.550
I thought that was crazy.
我觉得那太疯狂了。

490
00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:13.810
And so we were reminded that I could not wear a pantsuit.
所以我们被提醒我不能穿裤装套装。

491
00:21:14.030 --> 00:21:15.450
We had to keep the pencil skirt.
我们必须保留铅笔裙。

492
00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:18.850
So only thing we could change was the top half of my body.
所以我们唯一能改变的就是上半身。

493
00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:24.230
Who was the brass at the top of NBC that was like, office ladies must wear skirts?
到底是NBC高层的哪位大人物说“办公室女士必须穿裙子”的？

494
00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:26.810
Well, look at Phyllis, always in a skirt.
你看菲利斯，总是穿着裙子。

495
00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:28.890
Meredith, always in some kind of jumper.
梅雷迪斯，总是穿着某种连身裙。

496
00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:29.590
Kelly.
凯莉。

497
00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:30.190
Kelly.
凯莉。

498
00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:31.210
Jan.
简。

499
00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:34.530
And Nellie, skirts.
还有奈莉，也是裙子。

500
00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:37.630
However, Karen always wore pants.
不过，凯伦一直都穿裤子。

501
00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:39.130
I don't think she ever wore a skirt.
我觉得她好像从来没穿过裙子。

502
00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:41.750
And I think that sometimes Holly wore pants.
而且我觉得有时候霍莉会穿裤子。

503
00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:42.570
Am I right?
我没记错吧？

504
00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:45.810
But mostly, it was dresses and skirts.
但大部分时候，她穿的都是连衣裙和半身裙。

505
00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:47.410
Joe Bennett wore pants.
乔·贝内特穿的是裤子。

506
00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:49.190
But those were all guest stars.
但那些都是客串明星。

507
00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:51.870
Core Cast had to be in skirts, I guess.
我想核心演员必须得穿裙子。

508
00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:52.770
I don't know.
我也不清楚。

509
00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:54.750
Who was the network brass at the time?
当时电视台的高层是谁？

510
00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:56.570
The guy from Mad Men?
是《广告狂人》里的那个人吗？

511
00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:58.330
Was Don Draper running the network?
是唐·德雷珀在管理电视台吗？

512
00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:00.270
Is that who?
是他吗？

513
00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:01.250
Maybe.
也许吧。

514
00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:03.270
I feel a soapbox coming.
我觉得又要开始长篇大论了。

515
00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:04.750
No, I'm going to leave it.
不，我还是不说了。

516
00:22:04.810 --> 00:22:05.430
I'll leave it.
我不说了。

517
00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:06.270
Let's leave it.
我们还是别说了。

518
00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:07.530
Everyone knows it.
大家都知道。

519
00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:08.650
They heard it.
他们听到了。

520
00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:09.350
They heard it.
他们听到了。

521
00:22:09.350 --> 00:22:09.930
It was subtle.
这很微妙。

522
00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:10.410
It was there.
它就在那儿。

523
00:22:11.070 --> 00:22:13.690
Okay, so bottom line is, here's what we did.
好吧，总之，我们是这么做的。

524
00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:16.570
I switched out my pantyhose for tights.
我把丝袜换成了连裤袜。

525
00:22:17.070 --> 00:22:21.230
I'm wearing a little bit more of a heel, bit of a power shoe, and a blazer.
我穿了稍微高一点的跟鞋，那种气场鞋，还穿了件西装外套。

526
00:22:21.430 --> 00:22:23.850
So they were little changes, but they did feel impactful.
所以这些都是小改动，但确实感觉很有效果。

527
00:22:23.850 --> 00:22:26.870
I thought Pam felt a little more polished.
我觉得帕姆看起来更干练了一些。

528
00:22:27.170 --> 00:22:27.430
Yeah.
没错。

529
00:22:27.810 --> 00:22:28.650
That was our goal.
那就是我们的目标。

530
00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:32.230
Well, Michael is going to start his first day of work in a bathrobe.
迈克尔第一天上班时穿着睡袍。

531
00:22:32.470 --> 00:22:35.250
Pam's like, Michael, you were expecting me, weren't you?
帕姆说，迈克尔，你是在等我，对吧？

532
00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:36.070
He's like, yeah.
他说，是啊。

533
00:22:36.550 --> 00:22:36.890
Yeah.
是啊。

534
00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:39.570
She's like, are you wearing anything under the robe?
她说，你睡袍下面穿衣服了吗？

535
00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:41.110
And he's like, that's inappropriate.
他说，这太不合适了。

536
00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:49.130
He brings her inside, and he actually has set up his dining room sort of office-like.
他把她带进屋，还真的把餐厅布置得像个办公室一样。

537
00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:49.830
It's nice.
挺不错的。

538
00:22:50.190 --> 00:22:50.830
It is nice.
确实不错。

539
00:22:50.830 --> 00:22:55.130
I think these are all items he took from the supply chest as he was leaving, clearly.
我觉得这些东西显然都是他离开时从办公用品柜里拿走的。

540
00:22:55.490 --> 00:22:57.470
And he starts making French toaSt.
然后他开始做法式吐司。

541
00:22:58.050 --> 00:22:59.830
A lot of French toaSt.
做了好多法式吐司。

542
00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:06.250
And there was a deleted Pam talking head where she explains her motivation to join Michael.
还有一段被删减的帕姆采访，她解释了加入迈克尔公司的动机。

543
00:23:06.250 --> 00:23:10.030
She steps outside on the patio while he's making French toaSt.
在他做吐司的时候，她走到露台上。

544
00:23:10.250 --> 00:23:10.750
Here it is.
就是这段。

545
00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:12.870
I felt ready for a change.
我觉得自己准备好迎接改变了。

546
00:23:13.430 --> 00:23:19.510
After all these years at Dunder Mifflin, I just wasn't getting the same rush that I used to get from being a receptioniSt.
在邓德·米夫林工作了这么多年，做前台已经不能再给我带来以前那种兴奋感了。

547
00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:21.350
This feels good.
这种感觉真好。

548
00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:23.890
This egg won't crack.
这鸡蛋怎么敲不开。

549
00:23:24.270 --> 00:23:24.570
Oh.
噢。

550
00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:25.370
Okay.
好吧。

551
00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:29.040
The egg won't crack.
鸡蛋打不开。

552
00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:29.520
Yeah.
是啊。

553
00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:32.500
He interrupts her to help him crack eggs.
他打断她，让她帮他打鸡蛋。

554
00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:34.800
Pam enjoys her French toaSt.
帕姆很享受她的法式吐司。

555
00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:36.120
It was very good.
味道非常好。

556
00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:36.780
I ate it.
我把它吃掉了。

557
00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:37.780
Did you really?
真的吗？

558
00:23:37.780 --> 00:23:38.520
It was delicious.
太美味了。

559
00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:40.700
That was just real.
那可是真吃啊。

560
00:23:40.960 --> 00:23:42.080
Way to go, prop food.
干得好，道具食物。

561
00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:42.720
I know.
我知道。

562
00:23:42.860 --> 00:23:47.380
We had a fan question from Isla H, who said, who had to make all the French toast?
我们收到一个来自Isla H的粉丝提问，她问，到底是谁做了所有的法式吐司？

563
00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:49.160
Phil Shea and his team.
是菲尔·谢伊和他的团队。

564
00:23:49.480 --> 00:23:50.860
They made a bunch of French toaSt.
他们做了好多法式吐司。

565
00:23:51.020 --> 00:23:52.000
But here's the problem.
但问题在于。

566
00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:54.080
Michael won't stop making French toaSt.
迈克尔停不下来地做着法式吐司。

567
00:23:54.720 --> 00:24:02.100
And Pam realizes it's because he's having some feelings about really getting started in this new company.
帕姆意识到这是因为他在面对新公司起步时产生了一些情绪。

568
00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:08.500
She tries to get him to stop mixing the eggs, and it ends up spilling eggs all over him.
她试图让他停止搅拌鸡蛋，结果鸡蛋洒了他一身。

569
00:24:08.700 --> 00:24:11.200
All over him and into his crocs.
洒了他一身，还流进了他的洞洞鞋里。

570
00:24:11.400 --> 00:24:12.800
We got questions about that.
我们收到了关于那场戏的问题。

571
00:24:12.940 --> 00:24:15.520
People wanted to know, was it real egg in the bowl?
大家想知道，碗里的是真鸡蛋吗？

572
00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:19.220
Was the line, I have egg in my crocs, improvised?
“我的洞洞鞋里有鸡蛋”这句台词是即兴发挥的吗？

573
00:24:19.220 --> 00:24:23.440
And people were also curious, how did we do this scene?
大家还很好奇，我们是怎么拍这场戏的？

574
00:24:23.440 --> 00:24:28.460
Because it seems difficult to have the egg go in the same place each time.
因为要让鸡蛋每次都洒在同一个地方似乎很难。

575
00:24:28.660 --> 00:24:33.060
Well, I will say that Steve did improvise the line, I have egg in my crocs.
嗯，我可以肯定地说，史蒂夫确实即兴说了“我的洞洞鞋里有鸡蛋”这句台词。

576
00:24:34.600 --> 00:24:38.160
It was very hard not to laugh, but it's true.
当时忍住不笑真的很难，但这是真的。

577
00:24:38.760 --> 00:24:44.500
We couldn't get the egg to splash in the same way every time, so I could not laugh because this was a one-er.
我们无法让鸡蛋每次都以同样的方式溅出来，所以我不能笑，因为这是一镜到底的。

578
00:24:44.700 --> 00:24:46.320
We would have to use a whole take.
我们必须用掉整个拍摄条。

579
00:24:46.480 --> 00:24:49.200
We couldn't cut between different takes because the egg would be different.
我们不能在不同的拍摄条之间剪辑，因为鸡蛋的状态会不一样。

580
00:24:49.460 --> 00:24:50.820
Oh, so much pressure.
噢，压力太大了。

581
00:24:51.060 --> 00:24:53.020
It's so hard to not laugh with Steve.
和史蒂夫对戏时忍住不笑真的太难了。

582
00:24:53.260 --> 00:24:53.740
I know.
我懂。

583
00:24:53.960 --> 00:24:54.860
But I didn't.
但我忍住了。

584
00:24:54.940 --> 00:24:58.780
But I think you can tell how hard I am trying not to laugh in the scene.
但我觉得你能看出我在那场戏里忍得有多辛苦。

585
00:24:58.780 --> 00:25:00.160
Do you look constipated or something?
你看上去像便秘了吗？

586
00:25:00.160 --> 00:25:00.880
Yeah, I do.
是啊，确实像。

587
00:25:01.080 --> 00:25:04.460
I look like, you can tell I'm like tensely holding in.
我看起来……你能看出我当时在极力克制。

588
00:25:04.580 --> 00:25:05.460
It works, though.
不过效果很好。

589
00:25:05.620 --> 00:25:11.720
It just looks like Pam is like watching someone who she thinks is supposed to know what they're doing, who clearly doesn't.
看起来就像帕姆在看着一个她以为应该知道自己在做什么的人，但对方显然根本不知道。

590
00:25:11.820 --> 00:25:12.580
She's like, oh, crap.
她心想，糟了。

591
00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:13.700
What have I gotten myself into?
我这是上了什么贼船？

592
00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:20.160
Well, we did do several takes of this, and it was a big reset every time because we would have to clean up all the eggs in the kitchen.
我们确实拍了好几条，每次都要重置，因为我们得清理厨房里所有的鸡蛋。

593
00:25:20.160 --> 00:25:22.120
We'd have to clean up all the eggs on Steve.
我们得清理史蒂夫身上所有的鸡蛋。

594
00:25:22.120 --> 00:25:26.100
Steve, he would have to change his bathrobe, but this one was perfect.
史蒂夫得换掉他的浴袍，但这一条拍得太完美了。

595
00:25:26.100 --> 00:25:30.440
This was the time he improvised that line, and the egg just went everywhere.
就在那一次，他即兴说了那句台词，鸡蛋也溅得到处都是。

596
00:25:30.860 --> 00:25:34.460
So I also knew as I was standing there, this is the one.
所以我站在那里的时候就知道，就是这一条了。

597
00:25:35.020 --> 00:25:36.260
Do not mess this up.
千万别搞砸了。

598
00:25:36.440 --> 00:25:36.620
Right.
没错。

599
00:25:36.620 --> 00:25:44.960
So one thing to point out, you guys, which I love about our show, to nerd out on you for a minute, since Steve improvised the line, eggs in my Crocs,
所以有一点要指出，伙计们，这也是我喜欢我们剧的地方，让我稍微钻研一下细节，既然史蒂夫即兴说了“我的洞洞鞋里有鸡蛋”，

600
00:25:45.100 --> 00:25:49.100
that meant our camera operator had to improvise the move to pan down to his feet.
这意味着我们的摄影师必须即兴做出反应，把镜头摇向他的脚。

601
00:25:49.300 --> 00:25:49.600
Yes.
没错。

602
00:25:49.600 --> 00:25:52.320
That wouldn't have been planned, but that sells the joke.
那应该不是计划好的，但那让笑点更突出了。

603
00:25:52.640 --> 00:25:53.720
So good.
太棒了。

604
00:25:53.960 --> 00:25:55.120
Such a great two-hander.
真是精彩的双人戏。

605
00:25:55.380 --> 00:25:59.460
We also had a fan catch in this scene in the kitchen.
我们在这场厨房戏里还被粉丝抓到了一个细节。

606
00:25:59.940 --> 00:26:00.820
Sierra G.
Sierra G.

607
00:26:01.140 --> 00:26:02.060
and Lauren W.
和 Lauren W.

608
00:26:02.400 --> 00:26:08.920
point out that at 4 minutes 31 seconds, there's a sign on his kitchen counter that says, his.
指出在4分31秒时，他厨房台面上有一个写着“他的”的牌子。

609
00:26:09.500 --> 00:26:09.960
Yeah.
是啊。

610
00:26:10.200 --> 00:26:11.500
But there is no hers.
但没有“她的”。

611
00:26:11.980 --> 00:26:13.040
I saw that, too.
我也看到了。

612
00:26:13.040 --> 00:26:16.540
And they were like, I guess Jan took the hers when she left.
他们就说，我猜简离开的时候把“她的”带走了。

613
00:26:17.120 --> 00:26:19.880
Or maybe she never even wanted hers out.
或者也许她根本就没想把“她的”拿出来。

614
00:26:20.620 --> 00:26:22.420
Maybe Michael just bought a his.
也许迈克尔只买了一个“他的”。

615
00:26:22.600 --> 00:26:25.140
I think he bought a his, her, and she never put hers out.
我觉得他买了一套“他的”和“她的”，但她从没把“她的”摆出来。

616
00:26:25.360 --> 00:26:25.920
I don't know.
我不知道。

617
00:26:26.080 --> 00:26:28.080
It's sad no matter how it shook out.
不管真相如何，这都挺让人难过的。

618
00:26:28.320 --> 00:26:31.620
Should we go back to the office and see what's happening back there?
我们要回到办公室看看那边发生了什么吗？

619
00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:35.200
Yes, because this was a really fun conference room scene.
好啊，因为这真是一场很有趣的会议室戏。

620
00:26:35.200 --> 00:26:38.240
We were having an absolute blast with Idris.
我们和伊德里斯在一起玩得特别开心。

621
00:26:38.580 --> 00:26:45.340
He's holding court the way Michael used to, and he's telling them how things are going to proceed now that they've lost two employees.
他像以前的迈克尔一样掌控全场，告诉大家在失去两名员工后，接下来的工作该如何进行。

622
00:26:46.160 --> 00:26:48.760
But Kelly and Angela just want to know more about Charles.
但凯莉和安吉拉只想多了解查尔斯。

623
00:26:49.540 --> 00:26:52.580
I love that Kelly's like, where are you staying in Scranton?
我喜欢凯莉问他，你住在斯克兰顿哪里？

624
00:26:52.880 --> 00:26:53.980
And he's like, a hotel.
他回答说，酒店。

625
00:26:54.120 --> 00:26:55.720
And Angela goes, where were you born?
然后安吉拉问，你出生在哪里？

626
00:26:56.260 --> 00:26:57.400
Where were you born?
你出生在哪里？

627
00:26:57.580 --> 00:26:58.540
It was so fun.
太好玩了。

