他说，我不知道。

941
00:39:46.380 --> 00:39:48.880
Let's give credit to the whole writing staff.
就把功劳归给整个编剧组吧。

942
00:39:49.160 --> 00:39:52.340
Like some sort of collective genius came up with this line.
就像某种集体智慧想出了这句台词一样。

943
00:39:52.500 --> 00:39:54.360
But someone wrote that.
但肯定有人写过。

944
00:39:54.360 --> 00:39:55.800
From the office.
来自办公室的。

945
00:39:56.280 --> 00:39:56.640
Brilliant.
太天才了。

946
00:39:56.640 --> 00:39:58.120
And it's so good.
而且真的太棒了。

947
00:39:58.380 --> 00:40:02.480
And then last week we talked about Vikram having this amazing talking head.
上周我们还聊到维克拉姆有个很棒的采访镜头。

948
00:40:02.600 --> 00:40:03.260
That got deleted.
被删掉了。

949
00:40:03.380 --> 00:40:04.040
That got deleted.
被删掉了。

950
00:40:04.260 --> 00:40:05.800
This is where it would have lived, you guys.
伙计们，这本该是它出现的地方。

951
00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:11.940
Right after the scene in the car where he says this amazing proverb, he would have said,
就在车里他说出那句绝妙谚语的场景之后，他本该接着说，

952
00:40:12.060 --> 00:40:15.760
when you put your telemarketing career on the line, you're not putting much on the line.
当你把电话营销的职业生涯拿去冒险时，其实你也没冒多大险。

953
00:40:16.400 --> 00:40:18.620
And Ranjit was just perfection.
兰吉特简直太完美了。

954
00:40:18.980 --> 00:40:19.500
Everything.
方方面面。

955
00:40:19.820 --> 00:40:20.920
His delivery.
他的台词表现力。

956
00:40:21.160 --> 00:40:23.060
I just, I couldn't get enough of him.
我真是，怎么看都看不够他。

957
00:40:23.060 --> 00:40:24.740
Well, you just so believe him.
嗯，你就是会对他深信不疑。

958
00:40:24.960 --> 00:40:25.100
Yeah.
是啊。

959
00:40:25.300 --> 00:40:27.460
And our guest actors were always that way.
我们的客串演员总是这样。

960
00:40:27.600 --> 00:40:33.420
Alison Jones had this amazing ability to find people who didn't seem like they were acting at all.
艾莉森·琼斯有一种神奇的能力，能找到那些看起来根本不像是在演戏的人。

961
00:40:33.720 --> 00:40:34.000
Yeah.
没错。

962
00:40:34.440 --> 00:40:37.220
Well, Michael is going to go into the bowling alley.
迈克尔要走进保龄球馆了。

963
00:40:37.360 --> 00:40:38.940
He wants a pair of nine shoes.
他想要一双九号的鞋。

964
00:40:39.420 --> 00:40:41.380
Guess who's working the counter?
猜猜谁在柜台工作？

965
00:40:42.040 --> 00:40:42.380
Ryan.
瑞安。

966
00:40:42.860 --> 00:40:44.820
Ryan, who's not on the liSt.
瑞安，他可不在名单上。

967
00:40:47.760 --> 00:40:52.160
You know, Vikram has this great line in the car where he's like, he's been gone a long time.
你知道，维克拉姆在车里有句很棒的台词，他说他已经离开很久了。

968
00:40:52.160 --> 00:40:53.800
Is it possible he went bowling?
有没有可能他去打保龄球了？

969
00:40:54.080 --> 00:40:55.620
You know him better than I do.
你比我更了解他。

970
00:40:56.020 --> 00:41:00.740
And I thought, Jenna, your delivery as Pam was so great when you're like, yeah.
我当时想，珍娜，你演帕姆时的表现太棒了，就是你说“是啊”的时候。

971
00:41:00.740 --> 00:41:01.540
Yeah.
是啊。

972
00:41:01.560 --> 00:41:01.880
Yeah.
没错。

973
00:41:02.360 --> 00:41:08.420
So Pam goes in and sees what's happening and says, this was not on the list, Michael.
所以帕姆走进去看到发生了什么，说：“迈克尔，这不在名单上。”

974
00:41:08.660 --> 00:41:13.260
And then she looks at the list and then she's like, when did you put this on the list?
然后她看了看名单，又问：“你是什么时候把它加到名单上的？”

975
00:41:13.780 --> 00:41:14.880
I loved that.
我太喜欢那段了。

976
00:41:15.480 --> 00:41:19.880
We notice right away that Ryan is very tan and very blonde.
我们立刻注意到瑞安晒得很黑，头发也染成了金色。

977
00:41:20.140 --> 00:41:21.580
I was really curious.
我当时特别好奇。

978
00:41:21.580 --> 00:41:24.160
When did BJ know he was going to have to do this with his hair?
BJ是什么时候知道他得把头发弄成这样的？

979
00:41:24.740 --> 00:41:26.600
This is what he said on the DVD commentary.
这是他在DVD评论音轨里说的。

980
00:41:27.360 --> 00:41:32.340
So when I was in Germany and wasn't able to be on the show for a while, my character ran off to Thailand.
当时我在德国，有一段时间没法参加节目录制，我的角色就跑去泰国了。

981
00:41:32.580 --> 00:41:36.360
All I knew about Ryan coming back was that he was going to be blonde.
关于瑞安回归，我只知道他会变成金发。

982
00:41:36.720 --> 00:41:37.460
Now the tan.
至于晒黑。

983
00:41:37.680 --> 00:41:38.700
The tan is great, too.
晒黑的效果也很棒。

984
00:41:38.800 --> 00:41:39.700
The tan is very funny.
晒黑这个梗非常搞笑。

985
00:41:40.660 --> 00:41:43.120
I heard of the hair as frosted tips.
我听说那发型叫“挑染发尖”。

986
00:41:43.260 --> 00:41:46.640
And then when we did it, Mindy, whose idea it was, came in and was like, no, no, no.
后来我们做的时候，明迪——这主意是她出的——走过来说：“不，不，不。”

987
00:41:47.020 --> 00:41:48.280
We're only going to go for this joke once.
这个梗我们只能用一次。

988
00:41:48.380 --> 00:41:49.380
You have to be completely blonde.
你必须得把头发全染成金色。

989
00:41:49.840 --> 00:41:50.760
And so we dyed it.
于是我们就把它染了。

990
00:41:50.760 --> 00:41:54.700
And I wore a hat in public for weeks trying to save the surprise and save my dignity.
为了保密并挽回尊严，我在公共场合戴了好几周的帽子。

991
00:41:56.720 --> 00:42:01.960
And he goes on to say that he was also touring stand-up during this time.
他接着说，那段时间他还在进行单口喜剧巡演。

992
00:42:02.440 --> 00:42:07.680
So he got a spray-in brown coloring, you know, that you could like dot.
所以他买了一种喷雾式的棕色染发剂，你知道，就是那种可以点涂的。

993
00:42:07.960 --> 00:42:13.420
And so he sprayed his hair brown and then he went on stage and it started coming off.
他把头发喷成棕色，然后上台表演，结果染发剂开始往下掉。

994
00:42:13.600 --> 00:42:14.890
Like dripping off.
就像滴下来一样。

995
00:42:15.500 --> 00:42:17.440
Like what happened to Rudy Giuliani.
就像鲁迪·朱利安尼发生的那样。

996
00:42:18.060 --> 00:42:18.920
Oh, my God.
天哪。

997
00:42:19.480 --> 00:42:20.360
Same thing.
一模一样。

998
00:42:20.760 --> 00:42:22.360
Yes, exactly.
没错，就是那样。

999
00:42:22.700 --> 00:42:25.480
So he had to wear this hat, but it was like really stressful.
所以他不得不戴着那顶帽子，但这真的压力很大。

1000
00:42:25.480 --> 00:42:26.940
He was trying to keep it a secret.
他当时正试图保守这个秘密。

1001
00:42:27.380 --> 00:42:31.740
I've used that spray for when my roots are coming in.
我用过那种喷雾，就是发根长出来的时候。

1002
00:42:32.280 --> 00:42:33.340
It's genius.
简直是天才发明。

1003
00:42:33.340 --> 00:42:35.280
I love the spray, by the way.
顺便说一句，我超爱那个喷雾。

1004
00:42:35.460 --> 00:42:35.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1005
00:42:35.860 --> 00:42:36.400
It's great.
真的很棒。

1006
00:42:36.660 --> 00:42:40.880
But if you get really warm, it will sweat off.
但如果你出汗多的话，它会掉色的。

1007
00:42:41.080 --> 00:42:41.500
Yeah.
没错。

1008
00:42:42.040 --> 00:42:42.560
Beware.
小心点。

1009
00:42:43.980 --> 00:42:45.060
Where are we?
我们现在在哪儿？

1010
00:42:45.060 --> 00:42:48.100
I'll give you a little location breakdown on the bowling alley.
我来给你们简单介绍一下保龄球馆的取景地。

1011
00:42:48.760 --> 00:42:53.500
Idle Our Lanes, which is the sign-out sign, is a real bowling alley in Scranton.
“Idle Our Lanes”——就是那个挂着招牌的地方，是斯克兰顿真实存在的保龄球馆。

1012
00:42:53.660 --> 00:42:55.300
We matched their logo.
我们复刻了他们的标志。

1013
00:42:55.920 --> 00:42:58.260
And in Scranton, there's two.
斯克兰顿有两家这样的球馆。

1014
00:42:58.260 --> 00:43:01.200
And one of them is next to Poor Richard's.
其中一家就在“可怜理查德”酒吧旁边。

1015
00:43:01.780 --> 00:43:02.140
Yes.
是的。

1016
00:43:02.280 --> 00:43:03.360
I've been to that one.
我去过那家。

1017
00:43:03.440 --> 00:43:04.280
I thought you had.
我就猜你去过。

1018
00:43:04.440 --> 00:43:05.980
It's part of the bar, kind of.
它算是酒吧的一部分吧。

1019
00:43:06.060 --> 00:43:09.760
Like when you go into Poor Richard's, you think, at least I thought I was walking into a bar,
就像你走进“可怜理查德”时，你以为，至少我以为我是走进了一家酒吧，

1020
00:43:09.820 --> 00:43:13.000
but I actually was walking into a bowling alley and then the bar was to the right.
但其实我走进的是保龄球馆，酒吧在右边。

1021
00:43:13.560 --> 00:43:14.380
It's interesting.
挺有意思的。

1022
00:43:14.640 --> 00:43:21.240
I thought that we were at Pickwick Bowl, which does have a bar next to it, sort of similar to
我本来以为我们是在Pickwick保龄球馆拍的，那儿旁边也有个酒吧，跟

1023
00:43:21.240 --> 00:43:22.500
the real Idle Our Lanes.
真正的“Idle Our Lanes”有点像。

1024
00:43:22.660 --> 00:43:27.440
But no, Randy Cordray said that we shot ours in Canoga Park.
但并不是，兰迪·科德雷说我们是在卡诺加公园拍的。

1025
00:43:27.640 --> 00:43:29.400
It was a bowling alley in Canoga Park.
那是卡诺加公园的一家保龄球馆。

1026
00:43:29.640 --> 00:43:35.580
I also have a little guest star shout-out to the bowling alley manager who calls Ryan a
我还要特别提一下那位客串的保龄球馆经理，他管瑞安叫

1027
00:43:35.580 --> 00:43:36.180
shoe bitch.
“鞋子婊子”。

1028
00:43:37.100 --> 00:43:39.200
He was played by Jim Woods.
他是由吉姆·伍兹饰演的。

1029
00:43:39.200 --> 00:43:44.780
He has appeared on How I Met Your Mother, Reno 911, and was a regular on the comedy satire
他曾出演过《老爸老妈浪漫史》、《雷诺911》，还是喜剧讽刺剧

1030
00:43:44.780 --> 00:43:47.180
Safety Geeks, S-V-I.
《安全极客》（Safety Geeks, S-V-I）的常驻演员。

1031
00:43:47.880 --> 00:43:51.740
Again, another person who did not seem like an actor to me.
又是一个看起来完全不像演员的人。

1032
00:43:51.920 --> 00:43:52.280
Yeah.
没错。

1033
00:43:52.460 --> 00:43:55.920
Seemed like a real grouchy bowling alley manager.
看起来就像个真正的暴躁保龄球馆经理。

1034
00:43:56.360 --> 00:43:56.780
Exactly.
确实。

1035
00:43:57.220 --> 00:44:01.480
There was some delicious Pam sass because, I mean, Pam just does not like Ryan.
帕姆的表现真是太毒舌了，毕竟，帕姆就是不喜欢瑞安。

1036
00:44:01.820 --> 00:44:02.120
Mm-mm.
嗯。

1037
00:44:02.280 --> 00:44:06.240
When he tells her he makes 60 grand a year and she's like, really?
当瑞安告诉她他年薪六万时，她的反应是：真的吗？

1038
00:44:06.240 --> 00:44:09.820
They pay you a yearly salary at the bowling alley.
保龄球馆还给你发年薪啊。

1039
00:44:10.060 --> 00:44:10.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1040
00:44:10.640 --> 00:44:11.220
So good.
太精彩了。

1041
00:44:12.020 --> 00:44:15.920
Well, the Dream Team is going to arrive to meet their investor.
好了，“梦之队”要去见他们的投资人了。

1042
00:44:16.380 --> 00:44:17.100
That's right.
没错。

1043
00:44:17.480 --> 00:44:20.320
It's at what appears to be a nursing home.
地点看起来像是一家养老院。

1044
00:44:20.680 --> 00:44:25.020
Can I tell you there was a beat in the script where Michael describes who the investor is?
我能告诉你吗，剧本里原本有一段迈克尔描述投资人身份的戏份？

1045
00:44:25.400 --> 00:44:25.960
Okay.
好啊。

1046
00:44:26.300 --> 00:44:28.720
He says her name is Barbara Kivas.
他说她叫芭芭拉·基瓦斯。

1047
00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:33.800
She invests in local businesses and I've been putting together a little presentation for her.
她投资当地企业，我一直在为她准备一份简短的演示文稿。

1048
00:44:34.040 --> 00:44:34.440
Oh.
哦。

1049
00:44:34.440 --> 00:44:38.840
But that didn't make it in the episode, but I'm like, okay, who's Barbara Kivas?
但那段没剪进正片里，我当时就在想，好吧，芭芭拉·基瓦斯是谁？

1050
00:44:39.240 --> 00:44:41.860
I've got a location breakdown on where we shot this.
关于这场戏的拍摄地，我也有个简单的介绍。

1051
00:44:41.980 --> 00:44:42.240
Oh.
哦。

1052
00:44:42.540 --> 00:44:43.740
Which is interesting to me.
这对我来说很有意思。

1053
00:44:43.860 --> 00:44:50.320
It was a Best Western Hotel that was attached to the bowling alley and we redressed their conference
那是一家连着保龄球馆的贝斯特韦斯特酒店，我们重新布置了他们的会议室，

1054
00:44:50.320 --> 00:44:52.980
room to look like a nursing home.
让它看起来像一家养老院。

1055
00:44:54.000 --> 00:44:59.840
Randy Cordray said that our location manager, Kyle Alexander, was really awesome, that he would
兰迪·科德雷说我们的外景经理凯尔·亚历山大真的很棒，他说他

1056
00:44:59.840 --> 00:45:01.260
do this kind of thing all the time.
经常做这种事。

1057
00:45:01.260 --> 00:45:08.520
If we had an episode that had two locations, he would somehow manage to find them right next
如果我们有一集戏需要两个拍摄地点，他总能设法找到紧挨着的两个地方，

1058
00:45:08.520 --> 00:45:12.600
to each other so that we could avoid having to do what they call a company move.
这样我们就能避免进行所谓的“剧组大搬迁”。

1059
00:45:12.880 --> 00:45:13.020
Right.
没错。

1060
00:45:13.100 --> 00:45:14.980
We have to move all the trailers, all the people.
我们得搬动所有的拖车和所有的人员。

1061
00:45:15.320 --> 00:45:16.220
All the equipment.
所有的设备。

1062
00:45:16.580 --> 00:45:17.820
Saved so much time and money.
节省了大量的时间和金钱。

1063
00:45:17.940 --> 00:45:22.760
We were able to shoot the bowling alley and the nursing home all in one day.
我们得以在一天之内拍完了保龄球馆和养老院的戏份。

1064
00:45:22.760 --> 00:45:24.460
It saved so much money.
这省了很多钱。

1065
00:45:24.620 --> 00:45:26.020
It saved so much time.
这省了很多时间。

1066
00:45:26.540 --> 00:45:32.060
And Randy was just giving a lot of compliments to Kyle saying that Kyle was able to do this
兰迪对凯尔赞不绝口，说凯尔总是能做到这一点，

1067
00:45:32.060 --> 00:45:35.940
all the time and it was a huge, huge benefit to our production.
这对我们的制作来说是一个巨大的、巨大的优势。

1068
00:45:36.180 --> 00:45:36.660
Amazing.
太棒了。

1069
00:45:36.960 --> 00:45:42.180
And it was a benefit on a very practical level because it would save the time, which also
而且这在实际层面上也很有利，因为它节省了时间，

1070
00:45:42.180 --> 00:45:44.040
wouldn't run down the crew as much.
也不会让剧组人员那么疲惫。

1071
00:45:44.140 --> 00:45:52.220
And it also made it so that the actors, we could like flow from one experience sort of
这也让演员们能够从一种体验中顺畅地过渡，无论是

1072
00:45:52.220 --> 00:45:55.660
emotionally in the story and comedically right into another one.
在故事的情感上还是喜剧效果上，都能直接进入下一个场景。

1073
00:45:55.800 --> 00:45:57.040
We didn't have to stop.
我们不需要停下来。

1074
00:45:57.320 --> 00:45:58.920
It was awesome on many levels.
这在很多层面上都很棒。

1075
00:45:59.180 --> 00:46:00.220
Kyle, we love you.
凯尔，我们爱你。

1076
00:46:00.380 --> 00:46:01.100
Thank you, Kyle.
谢谢你，凯尔。

1077
00:46:01.100 --> 00:46:06.740
Kyle, I want to point out right as the Dream Team is entering the retirement home at 12
凯尔，我想指出的是，就在“梦之队”在12分钟时进入养老院的时候，

1078
00:46:06.740 --> 00:46:08.360
minutes, was it just me?
是我多心了吗？

1079
00:46:08.500 --> 00:46:14.760
Did anyone else notice the two like retirement home employees wheeling someone in a blanket?
还有人注意到那两个养老院员工推着一个盖着毯子的人吗？

1080
00:46:15.040 --> 00:46:15.720
I don't know.
我不知道。

1081
00:46:15.920 --> 00:46:18.660
Like, was it a corpse under a blanket?
那是毯子下面盖着一具尸体吗？

1082
00:46:18.920 --> 00:46:20.860
Oh my God, I did not notice that.
天哪，我没注意到。

1083
00:46:21.160 --> 00:46:26.320
I mean, I went over and over to it just like I couldn't stop looking at it.
我是说，我反复看了好几遍，就像我无法停止盯着它看一样。

1084
00:46:26.460 --> 00:46:28.420
I was like, who is this back there?
我在想，后面那个人是谁？

1085
00:46:28.620 --> 00:46:29.440
I'm going to show you, Jenna.
我要给你看，珍娜。

1086
00:46:29.620 --> 00:46:30.680
It's so brief.
镜头一闪而过。

1087
00:46:30.680 --> 00:46:32.440
But look, I don't know.
但你看，我不知道。

1088
00:46:32.520 --> 00:46:34.240
This person's like on a cut or a stretcher.
这人好像躺在担架或推车上。

1089
00:46:34.400 --> 00:46:34.960
Do you see?
你看到了吗？

1090
00:46:35.680 --> 00:46:36.180
Yes.
看到了。

1091
00:46:36.440 --> 00:46:37.820
I'll put it in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

1092
00:46:38.540 --> 00:46:44.300
My other background catch for this scene is at 12 minutes, 27 seconds, the elderly gentleman
我在这场戏里发现的另一个背景细节是，在12分27秒，那位老先生，

1093
00:46:44.300 --> 00:46:47.100
that Michael is like snapping like, hey, hey, over here.
迈克尔对他打响指说“嘿，嘿，看这边”。

1094
00:46:47.340 --> 00:46:49.320
He is watching Maury Povich.
他正在看《莫里·波维奇秀》。

1095
00:46:49.580 --> 00:46:49.840
Yes.
是的。

1096
00:46:49.840 --> 00:46:51.620
And it's actually Maury Povich.
