嗯。

1259
00:53:02.770 --> 00:53:03.950
There it makes contact.
就在那儿撞上了。

1260
00:53:04.170 --> 00:53:06.450
And then here you kind of see her face.
然后在这儿你能看到她的脸。

1261
00:53:06.750 --> 00:53:07.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1262
00:53:07.110 --> 00:53:09.170
Like she's kind of bending to the side.
就像她正往旁边歪一样。

1263
00:53:09.470 --> 00:53:10.190
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

1264
00:53:10.530 --> 00:53:11.530
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1265
00:53:11.750 --> 00:53:15.930
Phyllis did get hit with the ball in the episode where she gets hit with the ball.
菲利斯确实在被球砸的那一集里被球砸中了。

1266
00:53:16.050 --> 00:53:16.330
Yes.
是的。

1267
00:53:16.450 --> 00:53:17.290
And so did Kelly.
凯莉也是。

1268
00:53:17.570 --> 00:53:19.590
A lot of people were getting hit with the ball.
很多人都被球砸中了。

1269
00:53:20.190 --> 00:53:22.250
Well, we did also get some fan mail.
嗯，我们还收到了一些粉丝来信。

1270
00:53:22.430 --> 00:53:25.210
People wanted to know, did Phyllis perform her own stunt?
大家想知道，菲利斯是亲自上阵表演的特技吗？

1271
00:53:25.490 --> 00:53:27.250
Now, this is totally separate, guys.
现在，这完全是另一回事了，伙计们。

1272
00:53:27.530 --> 00:53:29.370
You know, what I just showed you was not-
你知道，我刚才给你们看的并不是——

1273
00:53:29.370 --> 00:53:29.670
No.
不是。

1274
00:53:29.890 --> 00:53:30.610
The scripted moment.
剧本里的那一幕。

1275
00:53:30.790 --> 00:53:31.770
Here's what happens.
事情是这样的。

1276
00:53:32.030 --> 00:53:36.830
There's this moment where Charles is going to kick the ball super hard
有这么一个瞬间，查尔斯准备用力把球踢向吉姆，

1277
00:53:36.830 --> 00:53:41.630
toward Jim, and Jim ducks, and Phyllis gets clocked in the face.
吉姆躲开了，结果菲利斯被球狠狠砸中了脸。

1278
00:53:41.710 --> 00:53:45.390
And everybody is like, Jim, why did you duck?
然后每个人都在问，吉姆，你为什么要躲？

1279
00:53:45.610 --> 00:53:45.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1280
00:53:46.030 --> 00:53:47.470
Dwight's like, Jim, why did you duck?
德怀特也说，吉姆，你为什么要躲？

1281
00:53:47.550 --> 00:53:50.090
An experienced soccer player wouldn't duck.
一个有经验的足球运动员是不会躲的。

1282
00:53:50.330 --> 00:53:56.030
First of all, I will tell you that there was no soccer ball used in this particular shot.
首先，我要告诉你们，在这个特定的镜头里根本没有足球。

1283
00:53:56.450 --> 00:53:59.790
Idris was kicking air, and Phyllis faked getting hit.
伊德里斯踢的是空气，而菲利斯是假装被砸中。

1284
00:54:00.030 --> 00:54:03.910
It is an amazing fakie hit.
那是一次非常精彩的假摔。

1285
00:54:04.150 --> 00:54:04.650
Yes.
没错。

1286
00:54:04.650 --> 00:54:09.410
Randy Cordray told me that we added the soccer ball using CGI magic.
兰迪·科德雷告诉我，我们是用CGI特效加上去的足球。

1287
00:54:09.750 --> 00:54:12.370
It was the folks at Stargate International.
是星际国际公司的人做的。

1288
00:54:12.770 --> 00:54:18.730
Randy actually said, I dare say it's one of the most effective uses of CGI that the office
兰迪甚至说，我敢说这是《办公室》用过的最有效的CGI特效之一。

1289
00:54:18.730 --> 00:54:19.950
ever incorporated.
真的。

1290
00:54:20.330 --> 00:54:22.370
I mean, it looks totally real.
我是说，看起来完全是真的。

1291
00:54:22.650 --> 00:54:27.590
Big applause to John for his, like, fakie seeing of the ball and ducking.
要为约翰鼓掌，他那种假装看到球并躲开的表演太棒了。

1292
00:54:27.810 --> 00:54:28.870
I mean, all of it.
我是说，所有的一切。

1293
00:54:28.970 --> 00:54:29.070
All of it.
所有的一切。

1294
00:54:29.070 --> 00:54:29.850
It all works.
效果都很好。

1295
00:54:30.130 --> 00:54:32.630
And then Phyllis is like, I think I swallowed a crown.
然后菲利斯说，我觉得我吞下了一颗牙冠。

1296
00:54:32.850 --> 00:54:33.490
I know.
我知道。

1297
00:54:33.490 --> 00:54:37.050
Oh, we also got a fan mail flurry.
哦，我们还收到了一大波粉丝来信。

1298
00:54:37.430 --> 00:54:38.470
What about?
关于什么的？

1299
00:54:38.810 --> 00:54:40.190
Jim ducking.
关于吉姆躲球的事。

1300
00:54:40.470 --> 00:54:43.170
Oh, is this a soccer fan mail flurry?
哦，这是一波关于足球的粉丝来信吗？

1301
00:54:43.410 --> 00:54:44.490
Like, soccer knowledge?
比如，足球知识？

1302
00:54:44.490 --> 00:54:44.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1303
00:54:44.990 --> 00:54:46.970
People coming to Jim's defense.
有人在为吉姆辩护。

1304
00:54:47.270 --> 00:54:47.570
Oh.
哦。

1305
00:54:48.410 --> 00:54:49.770
So, Ashley T.
所以，阿什莉·T.

1306
00:54:50.030 --> 00:54:55.330
said, I don't understand how Jim got blamed for this soccer ball hitting Phyllis
说，我不明白为什么吉姆要为那个足球击中菲利斯

1307
00:54:55.330 --> 00:54:55.890
in the face.
的脸而背锅。

1308
00:54:56.050 --> 00:54:57.770
Charles is the one who kicked it.
是查尔斯踢的球。

1309
00:54:58.110 --> 00:55:01.730
It's clearly Charles' fault because I would have ducked too.
这显然是查尔斯的错，因为换做是我也会躲开的。

1310
00:55:02.310 --> 00:55:03.090
Joseph F.
约瑟夫·F.

1311
00:55:03.270 --> 00:55:08.510
said, listen, I get it that maybe an experienced soccer player shouldn't have
说，听着，我明白也许一个有经验的足球运动员不应该

1312
00:55:08.510 --> 00:55:12.390
ducked, that they should have jumped up and intercepted the ball with their cheSt.
躲开，他们应该跳起来用胸部拦截足球。

1313
00:55:12.390 --> 00:55:20.010
However, Charles crossed the ball toward the side, in which case Jim and any other professional
然而，查尔斯把球传向了侧面，在这种情况下，吉姆和任何其他职业

1314
00:55:20.010 --> 00:55:21.650
player would have ducked.
球员都会躲开的。

1315
00:55:22.110 --> 00:55:22.630
Really?
真的吗？

1316
00:55:22.870 --> 00:55:23.010
Yes.
是的。

1317
00:55:23.010 --> 00:55:24.190
Because what, then the ball goes out?
因为什么，那样球就会出界吗？

1318
00:55:24.290 --> 00:55:25.070
I guess so.
我想是吧。

1319
00:55:25.150 --> 00:55:25.410
Oh.
哦。

1320
00:55:25.830 --> 00:55:26.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1321
00:55:26.690 --> 00:55:27.030
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1322
00:55:27.210 --> 00:55:27.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1323
00:55:27.890 --> 00:55:28.230
How about that?
那又怎样？

1324
00:55:28.230 --> 00:55:34.170
So, a fan mail flurry, lots of people commenting that Jim was not wrong for ducking.
所以，粉丝来信如雪片般飞来，很多人评论说吉姆躲开并没有错。

1325
00:55:34.390 --> 00:55:37.270
I do not know enough about soccer to comment.
我对足球了解不够，无法发表评论。

1326
00:55:37.670 --> 00:55:42.750
I don't either, even though I live on a soccer field every single Saturday with our kids.
我也不了解，尽管我每个周六都和孩子们待在足球场上。

1327
00:55:42.970 --> 00:55:44.170
Like, we're always there.
我们总是在那儿。

1328
00:55:44.190 --> 00:55:47.050
And my husband played soccer, and he's coaching soccer.
而且我丈夫踢过足球，他现在还在当足球教练。

1329
00:55:47.310 --> 00:55:49.030
I should have asked Josh about it.
我本该问问乔什关于这件事的。

1330
00:55:49.290 --> 00:55:53.470
Lee is coaching both of our kids' soccer teams this year.
李今年在执教我们两个孩子的足球队。

1331
00:55:53.630 --> 00:55:53.970
I know.
我知道。

1332
00:55:54.070 --> 00:55:56.030
Both of our husbands are soccer coaches this year.
我们两人的丈夫今年都是足球教练。

1333
00:55:56.030 --> 00:56:00.590
Yeah, and I just sit there, and I'm just trying to figure out offsides.
是啊，我只是坐在那儿，试图弄明白什么是越位。

1334
00:56:00.830 --> 00:56:02.030
I'll never figure it out.
我永远也弄不明白。

1335
00:56:02.150 --> 00:56:02.430
I still don't get it.
我到现在还是不懂。

1336
00:56:02.490 --> 00:56:03.130
I'll never figure it out.
我永远也弄不明白。

1337
00:56:03.130 --> 00:56:04.650
I don't think the kids get it.
我觉得孩子们也不懂。

1338
00:56:04.750 --> 00:56:05.010
No.
确实。

1339
00:56:05.130 --> 00:56:06.530
The referees call it.
裁判判罚就是了。

1340
00:56:06.690 --> 00:56:07.610
I don't get it.
我不懂。

1341
00:56:07.650 --> 00:56:08.490
I don't ever get it.
我永远也搞不懂。

1342
00:56:08.570 --> 00:56:09.910
I'm like, what happened, offsides?
我就像是在问，发生什么了，越位了吗？

1343
00:56:09.990 --> 00:56:10.190
What?
什么？

1344
00:56:10.410 --> 00:56:14.130
Listen, I've said in this episode that I don't know much about basketball.
听着，我在这一集里说过，我对篮球了解不多。

1345
00:56:14.150 --> 00:56:14.830
That's true.
那是真的。

1346
00:56:14.830 --> 00:56:16.350
I don't know a lot about soccer.
我对足球了解也不多。

1347
00:56:16.930 --> 00:56:20.250
But talk to me about, like, hockey, football, or baseball.
但如果是聊冰球、橄榄球或棒球，尽管找我。

1348
00:56:20.250 --> 00:56:22.390
You're very well-versed in hockey.
你对冰球确实非常精通。

1349
00:56:22.590 --> 00:56:23.570
I don't get hockey.
我不懂冰球。

1350
00:56:23.850 --> 00:56:24.670
I'm, like, into those sports.
我挺喜欢那些运动的。

1351
00:56:24.670 --> 00:56:26.410
It's a live hockey game.
这是一场现场冰球比赛。

1352
00:56:26.530 --> 00:56:27.410
There's nothing like it.
没有什么比这更棒的了。

1353
00:56:27.550 --> 00:56:29.370
I think it's the best sport to watch live.
我认为这是现场观看体验最好的运动。

1354
00:56:29.530 --> 00:56:31.750
Personally, I know people love watching basketball live.
就我个人而言，我知道人们很喜欢现场看篮球。

1355
00:56:31.950 --> 00:56:36.470
I mean, watching basketball live, especially if you can get close to the court, it's, like,
我是说，现场看篮球，尤其是如果你能坐得离球场很近的话，那真是，怎么说呢，

1356
00:56:36.830 --> 00:56:38.270
an amazing game live.
现场看比赛太棒了。

1357
00:56:38.570 --> 00:56:40.510
I just love the whole hockey community.
我就是喜欢整个冰球圈子。

1358
00:56:40.510 --> 00:56:41.950
I love everything about it.
我喜欢关于它的一切。

1359
00:56:42.110 --> 00:56:46.090
I went one time and met some of your hockey mom friends.
我有一次去现场，还见到了你的一些冰球妈妈朋友。

1360
00:56:46.230 --> 00:56:46.450
Yeah.
没错。

1361
00:56:46.650 --> 00:56:51.250
And what I didn't know, you guys, is that hockey games, they serve beer at 10 in the morning.
而且我不知道的是，伙计们，冰球比赛竟然在早上10点就供应啤酒。

1362
00:56:51.390 --> 00:56:51.750
They do.
确实如此。

1363
00:56:52.230 --> 00:56:53.450
I was like, oh, my gosh.
我当时心想，天哪。

1364
00:56:53.450 --> 00:56:54.110
They sure do.
他们确实供应。

1365
00:56:54.470 --> 00:56:56.390
We have, like, juice boxes at soccer.
我们看足球赛时喝的是果汁盒。

1366
00:56:56.650 --> 00:56:57.610
They have beer.
他们却喝啤酒。

1367
00:56:58.050 --> 00:57:03.850
I remember going to, like, one of our early hockey games for my son, and it was at 730
我记得有一次去参加我儿子早期的冰球比赛，时间是早上7点半，

1368
00:57:03.850 --> 00:57:05.730
in the morning, and I brought a coffee.
我带了一杯咖啡。

1369
00:57:06.150 --> 00:57:11.290
And people were like, does anyone want a beer from the concessions?
结果有人问，有人想从小卖部买啤酒吗？

1370
00:57:11.450 --> 00:57:14.950
And I was like, um, I don't think so, but thank you.
我当时就想，呃，我想不用了，但谢谢你。

1371
00:57:15.790 --> 00:57:16.650
Pretty amazing.
真是太神奇了。

1372
00:57:17.450 --> 00:57:22.970
Well, listen, the Dream Team has lost a member, and they get back to Michael's condo.
好了，听着，“梦之队”失去了一名成员，他们回到了迈克尔的公寓。

1373
00:57:23.530 --> 00:57:24.590
Ryan's going to run inside.
瑞安要跑进去。

1374
00:57:24.590 --> 00:57:27.090
He wants to watch the closer on TNT.
他想看TNT电视台播出的《结案高手》。

1375
00:57:27.490 --> 00:57:28.430
Very important to him.
这对我很重要。

1376
00:57:28.870 --> 00:57:30.550
Pam's upset she can't get out of the car.
帕姆很沮丧，因为她没法下车。

1377
00:57:30.730 --> 00:57:32.070
Now Pam's going to spiral.
现在帕姆要崩溃了。

1378
00:57:32.070 --> 00:57:33.390
So guess what?
所以你猜怎么着？

1379
00:57:33.630 --> 00:57:33.830
Hmm.
嗯。

1380
00:57:34.330 --> 00:57:36.690
It was not in the script that you stayed in the car.
剧本里并没有写你要待在车里。

1381
00:57:36.890 --> 00:57:37.590
I remember.
我记得。

1382
00:57:37.970 --> 00:57:44.110
It was Jen Salata's idea, and she fought for it to have Pam stay in the car during the scene.
那是简·萨拉塔的主意，她极力争取让帕姆在这一幕中留在车里。

1383
00:57:44.250 --> 00:57:44.410
Yeah.
没错。

1384
00:57:44.570 --> 00:57:49.970
I was supposed to get out of the car, and then sort of the idea was lean against it.
我本来应该下车的，然后大概的想法是靠在车边。

1385
00:57:50.130 --> 00:57:54.330
And part of that was because it would be really easy to stage it camera-wise.
部分原因是这样在摄影机调度上会非常容易。

1386
00:57:54.330 --> 00:57:54.690
Yeah.
没错。

1387
00:57:55.110 --> 00:58:00.310
Well, I loved her staying in the car, and I love this shot at 16 minutes, 22 seconds,
我喜欢她留在车里的安排，我也很喜欢16分22秒时的那个镜头，

1388
00:58:00.350 --> 00:58:05.350
when you see Pam in the side mirror and Michael standing next to the car.
你可以从侧视镜里看到帕姆，而迈克尔就站在车旁。

1389
00:58:05.530 --> 00:58:06.670
It's such a cool shot.
那是一个非常酷的镜头。

1390
00:58:06.930 --> 00:58:09.150
I had to bring a lot of emotion to this scene.
我必须为这一幕投入大量的情感。

1391
00:58:09.150 --> 00:58:13.970
You had to see Pam be convinced by Michael, and this is one of those moments when
你必须看到帕姆被迈克尔说服，而这正是其中一个时刻，

1392
00:58:13.970 --> 00:58:19.230
Michael becomes really good at being a boss.
迈克尔展现出了他作为老板非常出色的一面。

1393
00:58:19.390 --> 00:58:20.430
And he's so serious.
而且他表现得非常严肃。

1394
00:58:20.430 --> 00:58:21.570
He's like, listen, kiddo.
他说，听着，小姑娘。

1395
00:58:21.730 --> 00:58:22.050
Yeah.
没错。

1396
00:58:22.370 --> 00:58:22.930
You quit.
你辞职了。

1397
00:58:23.270 --> 00:58:24.050
I quit.
我辞职了。

1398
00:58:25.570 --> 00:58:27.110
So that's the truth.
事实就是这样。

1399
00:58:27.330 --> 00:58:33.990
It was very easy to get emotional because to have Steve Carell say, listen, kiddo, I mean,
要投入情感非常容易，因为当史蒂夫·卡瑞尔说“听着，小姑娘”时，我是说，

1400
00:58:34.130 --> 00:58:40.250
I know he wasn't much older than us, but he did always have sort of like a wise fatherly.
我知道他其实没比我们大多少，但他确实总是带有一种睿智的父爱感。

1401
00:58:40.250 --> 00:58:41.050
He was our mentor.
他是我们的导师。

1402
00:58:41.410 --> 00:58:41.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1403
00:58:42.070 --> 00:58:42.710
Like, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1404
00:58:43.010 --> 00:58:48.590
And so to have your mentor coach you, it felt real, you know?
所以能让自己的导师来指导自己，感觉真的很真实，你懂吗？

1405
00:58:48.790 --> 00:58:54.050
And it made me emotional, and we just really connected there in a real way.
这让我很感动，我们当时真的建立了一种真实的联结。

1406
00:58:54.050 --> 00:58:55.490
And it was really sweet.
真的很温馨。

1407
00:58:55.670 --> 00:58:59.630
I just love those Pam Michael moments that reminds me of when he came to her art show.
我特别喜欢那些帕姆和迈克尔的瞬间，让我想起他去参加她画展的时候。

1408
00:59:00.190 --> 00:59:01.830
And he shows up for her.
他总是会支持她。

1409
00:59:02.090 --> 00:59:02.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1410
00:59:02.470 --> 00:59:03.390
And it was great.
那真的很棒。

1411
00:59:03.390 --> 00:59:09.210
Well, next, we're going to see Michael on the phone, and he's asking Billy Merchant if
好了，接下来我们要看到迈克尔在打电话，他问比利·默钱特

1412
00:59:09.210 --> 00:59:13.970
he has any free office space anywhere because they can't work out of Michael's condo anymore.
有没有空余的办公空间，因为他们不能再在迈克尔的公寓里办公了。

1413
00:59:14.170 --> 00:59:15.290
They're going to throw him out.
他们要把他赶出去了。

1414
00:59:15.410 --> 00:59:16.070
They got a letter.
他们收到了一封信。

1415
00:59:16.070 --> 00:59:18.850
And Billy says, I got something for you.
然后比利说，我这儿有地方给你。

1416
00:59:19.070 --> 00:59:21.310
It's like a supply room, maybe.
大概像是个储藏室之类的。

1417
00:59:21.510 --> 00:59:23.330
But there's also like a shower.
但里面还有个淋浴间。

1418
00:59:23.690 --> 00:59:27.170
It's also back at the Dunder Mifflin Scranton building.
而且还是在邓德·米夫林斯克兰顿分公司的楼里。

1419
00:59:27.290 --> 00:59:27.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1420
00:59:27.790 --> 00:59:29.150
I probably should have led with that.
我本来应该先说这个的。

1421
00:59:30.470 --> 00:59:32.130
And that's exactly right.
你说得太对了。

1422
00:59:32.130 --> 00:59:34.490
It's like a supply room closet.
那就像个储藏室壁橱。

1423
00:59:35.150 --> 00:59:38.010
But the gang is like, I could work here.
但大家却觉得，我可以在这儿工作。

1424
00:59:38.010 --> 00:59:39.690
Yeah, they can see it.
没错，他们能看出潜力。

1425
00:59:39.930 --> 00:59:46.190
And it's really sweet because the episode ends with Michael adding Michael Scott Paper
这真的很温馨，因为剧集结尾是迈克尔把“迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司”

1426
00:59:46.190 --> 00:59:50.690
Company to the little board in the lobby, and Pam's handing him the little letters.
加到了大厅的小告示板上，帕姆递给他那些小字母。

1427
00:59:51.290 --> 00:59:56.470
Matt Sohn shared that there was a take where instead of you guys already having the letters,
马特·索恩分享说，有一个拍摄版本里，你们不是已经有了字母，

1428
00:59:56.710 --> 00:59:59.770
that you were taking the letters from other people's businesses' names.
而是从其他公司的名字里把字母抠下来。

1429
00:59:59.810 --> 01:00:00.250
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1430
01:00:00.250 --> 01:00:01.310
I remember that.
我记得那个。

1431
01:00:01.910 --> 01:00:03.090
I remember that.
我也记得。

1432
01:00:03.090 --> 01:00:04.630
Which is really funny to me.
我觉得那真的很有趣。

1433
01:00:04.910 --> 01:00:07.830
And there was a tag that didn't make it in the episode.
还有一个没被剪进正片的彩蛋。

1434
01:00:08.250 --> 01:00:09.810
Kevin is back at reception.
凯文回到了前台。

1435
01:00:10.090 --> 01:00:11.170
The phone rings.
电话响了。

1436
01:00:11.510 --> 01:00:13.070
Kevin answers it.
凯文接起电话。

1437
01:00:13.330 --> 01:00:17.050
And he's able to transfer the call to Dwight successfully.
他成功地把电话转接给了德怀特。

1438
01:00:17.390 --> 01:00:18.590
He's so happy.
他特别开心。

1439
01:00:18.750 --> 01:00:20.130
He looks all cocky to camera.
他对着镜头一脸得意。

1440
01:00:20.810 --> 01:00:24.490
Charles comes out and says, hey, Kevin, I need you to set up a conference call with David
查尔斯走出来说，嘿，凯文，我需要你十分钟后安排一场和大卫·华莱士

1441
01:00:24.490 --> 01:00:26.830
Wallace and the other branch managers in 10 minutes.
以及其他分公司经理的电话会议。

1442
01:00:27.010 --> 01:00:28.470
I'll take it in the conference room.
我会去会议室接听。

1443
01:00:28.770 --> 01:00:31.050
Kevin looks like he's going to crap his pants.
凯文看起来快要吓尿了。

1444
01:00:31.830 --> 01:00:33.430
He goes, you got it, boss.
他说，没问题，老板。

1445
01:00:33.670 --> 01:00:37.770
And then he runs out of the office and never comes back.
然后他就跑出了办公室，再也没回来。

1446
01:00:39.090 --> 01:00:44.730
You know, I asked Brian, what was it like to be at the reception desk for that week?
你知道吗，我问过布莱恩，在那一周坐在前台是什么感觉？

1447
01:00:44.950 --> 01:00:48.250
You know, because I noticed throughout the whole episode, he's in the background.
因为我注意到在整集里，他都在背景里。

1448
01:00:48.570 --> 01:00:52.530
And he was doing what I had to do, which is be in the background a lot.
他做着我以前必须做的事，那就是经常待在背景里。

1449
01:00:52.870 --> 01:00:57.670
And he did point out that just because you guys were in the corner, which is something
他确实指出，就因为你们当时被挤在角落里，这也是你们

1450
01:00:57.670 --> 01:01:03.210
you've talked about, you know, they would make you guys stand at the copier.
提到过的事，他们会让你们站在复印机旁边。

1451
01:01:03.490 --> 01:01:06.790
So he was just happy he got to sit for his background work.
所以他只是因为能坐着做背景工作就很高兴了。

1452
01:01:06.890 --> 01:01:09.270
I'm telling you, I stood for almost nine years.
我跟你说，我站了快九年了。

1453
01:01:09.470 --> 01:01:09.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1454
01:01:10.470 --> 01:01:11.410
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

1455
01:01:11.630 --> 01:01:13.070
Well, that was Dream Team.
好吧，那是梦之队。

1456
01:01:13.430 --> 01:01:15.610
Next up is Michael Scott Paper Company.
接下来是迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司。

1457
01:01:15.870 --> 01:01:18.970
We're going to get busy in that little storage room.
我们要在那间小储藏室里忙活起来了。

1458
01:01:19.330 --> 01:01:19.990
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1459
01:01:20.170 --> 01:01:20.550
Me too.
我也是。

1460
01:01:20.950 --> 01:01:21.230
All right.
好的。

1461
01:01:21.310 --> 01:01:22.450
Have a great week, you guys.
祝大家这周过得愉快。

1462
01:01:22.610 --> 01:01:23.190
See you then.
到时候见。

1463
01:01:23.190 --> 01:01:31.220
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

